{"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Shadowmasking is enabled. Directional shadows will be rendered with real-time shadows overlaid on top of the shadowmask texture. This mode makes for smoother shadow transitions when the camera moves fast, at the cost of a potential smearing effect for directional shadows that are up close (due to the real-time shadow being mixed with a low-resolution shadowmask). Objects that only have shadows baked in the shadowmask (and no real-time shadows) will keep their shadows up close.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/LightmapGIData\/ShadowmaskMode\/overlay"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"overlay"}],"symbolKind":"case","role":"symbol","title":"LightmapGIData.ShadowmaskMode.overlay","roleHeading":"Case","externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot14LightmapGIDataC14ShadowmaskModeO7overlayyA2EmF"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"overlay","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/lightmapgidata\/shadowmaskmode\/overlay"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/LightmapGIData","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/LightmapGIData\/ShadowmaskMode"]]},"references":{"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/LightmapGIData":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LightmapGIData","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/LightmapGIData","title":"LightmapGIData","abstract":[{"text":"Contains baked lightmap and dyna